/> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T02:19:12-07:00","id":199847,"title":"","content":"Satchel, it being more difficult to figure out an embed or exploit from a nonstandard use makes sense, so does it make more sense for it to be harder to pioneer a new exploit or embed by analyzing a near field effect, and for that matter it would also make more sense for it be harder to discover an embed or exploit with nonstandard options available so it being more difficult to reverse engineer near field effects in no ways exclude any of the possible scenarios here. <br /> <br /> At least with lambda gadgets one can make the obvious conclusion that demons can't multitask their powers like that, but embeds and exploits are basically the cheat codes of the universe, if a near field effect can do a trick and demons can't duplicate it, there needs to be a logically reason to answer &quot;why not?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:25:44-07:00","id":199992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/194206-near-field-effects-and-new-embeds?p=199847#post199847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least with lambda gadgets one can make the obvious conclusion that demons can't multitask their powers like that, but embeds and exploits are basically the cheat codes of the universe, if a near field effect can do a trick and demons can't duplicate it, there needs to be a logically reason to answer &quot;why not?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because <i>we have examples of the kinds of things it takes to generate a new Embed and they are a lot more involved than &quot;make a particularly strange single-power Gadget, take it apart, and watch the funny lights inside your head.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> If you can substitute two rolls and a risk of Aether-beaconing in a controlled environment for <i>breaking into God's house and messing with Its notes to make it write a new loophole into reality</i>, you have completely negated any point to doing the latter as a means of developing new Embeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}